{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-SA_TOKEN_DEFAULT-01","module":"iac","title":"Pod does not disable automatic service-account token mounting","severity":"medium","base_severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","cwe":"CWE-269","owasp":"A01:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/batch-check/job.yaml","match_digest":"5adb182c7eac659d","occurrence":"0","line":2},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/batch-check/job.yaml:2"},"evidence":"kind: Job","remediation":"Set automountServiceAccountToken to false on the pod spec (or the\nServiceAccount) unless the workload genuinely calls the Kubernetes API. The default is\ntrue, so every pod otherwise carries a live, mountable credential for its service\naccount into a container that most workloads never use it from - exactly what a\ncontainer-escape or SSRF exploit looks for next.","references":["CWE-269"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"972f26b12228894e2601b2f1ff564f37e5dd89072f92c0dc8f9df93988223820","fingerprint":"1b9968cb11b2ca17af476ba6ecd574237654a9c5495d2afefb806c220c40f7d2"}
