{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-MUTABLE_TAG-01","module":"iac","title":"Container image pinned to the mutable :latest tag","severity":"medium","base_severity":"medium","confidence":"high","cwe":"CWE-494","owasp":"A08:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/docker-bench-security/deployment.yaml","match_digest":"edb7206e07d709e3","occurrence":"0","line":35},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/docker-bench-security/deployment.yaml:35"},"evidence":"        image: busybox:latest","remediation":"Pin the image to an immutable reference - a specific semver tag the registry\nwill not overwrite, or better, a content-addressed digest (`@sha256:...`). `:latest`\n(or no tag at all, which defaults to it) means the same manifest can deploy a different\nimage tomorrow with no corresponding change to review, and a rollback cannot pin to\n\"what was actually running.\"","references":["CWE-494"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"f400803fd5afd0e08469b888f9d7e9a9174095b5aed8bd0ec7a20a132e873d07","fingerprint":"0b626c73573d74f5291c6723dd28d802a8c801c036cfce21c5218504419f5500"}
{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-SA_TOKEN_DEFAULT-01","module":"iac","title":"Pod does not disable automatic service-account token mounting","severity":"medium","base_severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","cwe":"CWE-269","owasp":"A01:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/docker-bench-security/deployment.yaml","match_digest":"18f00bdf678b235b","occurrence":"0","line":13},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/docker-bench-security/deployment.yaml:13"},"evidence":"kind: DaemonSet","remediation":"Set automountServiceAccountToken to false on the pod spec (or the\nServiceAccount) unless the workload genuinely calls the Kubernetes API. The default is\ntrue, so every pod otherwise carries a live, mountable credential for its service\naccount into a container that most workloads never use it from - exactly what a\ncontainer-escape or SSRF exploit looks for next.","references":["CWE-269"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"972f26b12228894e2601b2f1ff564f37e5dd89072f92c0dc8f9df93988223820","fingerprint":"0ab50324388b03bbc0bc0c326376fdcec2c8005eba08fe46fd64f8bb4228a136"}
